## <div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Renewable Energy – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Renewable Energy in Panama</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Why Is Renewable Energy Important for Panama?</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write reflective pieces on short stories. Interactive: Comment on peers' writing in various formats, including on paper and online.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a reflective paragraph explaining how Panama can benefit from renewable energy (e.g., "Panama can benefit from renewable energy because it can reduce pollution and save money." "Using wind farms as they do in Penonome can provide clean energy to rural areas and reduce the country's dependence on fossil fuels.")
Can comment on a peer's description of renewable energy sources (e.g., "I agree with your point about solar power. Another benefit is that it's available everywhere, even in remote areas.")
Can provide feedback on a group's project about energy-saving tips (e.g., "I like your ideas. Maybe you could also talk about using energy-efficient light bulbs to save more energy.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of images showing various renewable energy sources in Panama (e.g., Penonomé wind farm, hydroelectric dams, solar panels on a building). Students quickly brainstorm and write down 2-3 benefits of renewable energy they remember from previous lessons on sticky notes. They share one benefit with a partner, practicing vocabulary like "clean," "sustainable," "generate," and "preserve."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a sample sentence on the board, demonstrating the use of a gerund and an adverbial clause for justification related to the theme. For example: "<b>Saving</b> energy is essential for Panama <b>because</b> it preserves natural resources." The teacher highlights "Saving" and "because" and explains their function. Pronunciation focus: Teacher models stress in "renewable" and "preservation," then guides students to repeat.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"In 'Saving energy is essential,' is 'Saving' acting like a verb or a noun?" (Expected answer: A noun/the subject)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'because' tell us in the sentence 'Renewable energy is vital because it preserves natural resources'?" (Expected answer: It tells us the reason/why it's vital.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[____ / ____ / ____]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Approx. 10 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students receive a short informational text excerpt (approx. 80-100 words) from a simulated Panamanian environmental blog titled "Panama's Green Future." The text describes a local initiative using solar panels in a rural community and mentions the ongoing installation of wind turbines. The genre is informational/reflective, semi-formal register, presented as a written article.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Understanding information and opinions about renewable energy in Panama to prepare for written expression.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the main topic of this blog post?" "What specific renewable energy sources are mentioned?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match phrases from the text to complete sentences. Example: "Using solar energy ______." (A. saves money, B. pollutes the air). "The community is currently ______." (A. consuming fossil fuels, B. installing more panels).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students identify and underline all gerunds and present continuous verbs used in the text.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[____ / ____ / ____]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Approx. 10 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Using gerunds to describe environmental actions, using the present continuous for ongoing actions, and adverbial clauses for justification (because, since, as, due to). Vocabulary: energy, solar, wind, source, preservation, sustainability, generate, provide, emit, save, agree.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> Students complete sentences related to renewable energy using the correct form of verbs as gerunds or present continuous, and appropriate adverbial clauses. Example: "_____ (Reduce) our reliance on fossil fuels is important. Many countries _____ (invest) in clean energy now _____ (because) they want to protect the environment." (Teacher provides options for clauses: because, since, as a result of).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Expansion/Transformation):</b> Students work individually to expand simple sentences about renewable energy. For example, they transform "Solar power is clean" into a longer sentence using a gerund and an adverbial clause: "<b>Using</b> solar power is beneficial for Panama <b>because</b> it helps reduce air pollution." They also rephrase sentences using the present continuous, e.g., "Panama implements green projects" becomes "Panama <b>is currently implementing</b> many green energy projects."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Pre-writing & Peer Check:</b> In pairs, students create 3-4 sentences describing specific benefits of renewable energy in Panama. They must include at least one gerund, one present continuous verb, and one adverbial clause in their collective sentences. They then exchange their sentences with another pair for a quick grammar and vocabulary check before moving to individual writing.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[____ / ____ / ____]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Approx. 15 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual reflective paragraph writing followed by peer feedback (on paper).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Description:</b> Students will write a reflective paragraph (5-7 sentences) in response to the theme: "Why is renewable energy important for Panama?" Their paragraph must include:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least two gerunds (e.g., "Saving," "Generating").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least two instances of the present continuous (e.g., "We are installing," "Panama is developing").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least two adverbial clauses for justification (e.g., "because it reduces pollution," "since it's a clean source").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Relevant vocabulary from the unit (e.g., solar, wind, sustainable, environment, generate, preserve).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After writing, students exchange paragraphs with a peer. They read their peer's paragraph and provide written comments using pragmatic functions for feedback (e.g., "I agree with your point about solar power. Another benefit is that it's available everywhere, even in remote areas." or "I like your ideas. Maybe you could also talk about using energy-efficient light bulbs to save more energy.").</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[____ / ____ / ____]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Approx. 10 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher observation during writing and peer feedback, supported by a simple peer assessment checklist (checking for inclusion of target grammar and vocabulary in the peer's paragraph). The teacher collects both the original paragraphs and the peer feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students produce a reflective paragraph on the importance of renewable energy for Panama and provide constructive written feedback on a peer's paragraph.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher & Peer):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Paragraph clarity and coherence (A2.4 level).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (energy, solar, wind, generate, preserve, sustainable).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct usage of gerunds to describe environmental actions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct usage of the present continuous for ongoing actions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of adverbial clauses for justification (because, since, as).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to provide relevant and polite written feedback to a peer.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following prompts:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"On a scale of 1-5, how confidently did I use gerunds and adverbial clauses in my paragraph today?" (1 = not confident, 5 = very confident)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing I learned about giving helpful feedback to my classmates?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[____ / ____ / ____]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Approx. 5 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was challenging about writing my paragraph today, and what strategy did I use to overcome it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can using gerunds and adverbial clauses make my explanations about environmental issues clearer in English?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did the students effectively integrate the target grammar (gerunds, present continuous, adverbial clauses) into their reflective paragraphs? What were the most common grammatical or vocabulary errors, and how can I address them in future lessons?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How well did students provide constructive feedback to their peers, considering the pragmatic functions taught? Were there specific areas where more scaffolding for peer interaction is needed?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments are needed for Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration) to ensure students can successfully consolidate their knowledge and writing skills into a project on renewable energy in Panama?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5, students will utilize all the vocabulary, grammar, and communicative skills acquired throughout the unit, including their ability to write reflective pieces and provide feedback, to complete a larger project focusing on mediation and integration of information about renewable energy in Panama.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[____ / ____ / ____]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Approx. 5 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>